es control and gets really angry  giving the character a chance to finally  take the lid off and go toe-to-toe with  a hero who isn't Thor would satisfy a  question Marvel fans have wondered for  years could the Hulk be stopped by our  heroes and villains if they needed to  Thor knocked him out once and Tony Stark  won on a technicality but that was  before Bruce Banner embraced his big  green alter ego a Hulk that's both  savage and smart like the one we see in  world war hulk would be a lot more than  they bargained for there's a small but  vocal contingent of fans who believe the  Hulk didn't get his fair shake in the  movies adapting the World War Hulk  storyline could satisfy that group in a  big violent hurry Plus what's better  than a whole bunch of MCU hulk fights  nothing that's what  after the first guardians of the galaxy  movie dealt so heavily with the Nova  Corps many believed that the  introduction of Richard Ryder the  classic Nova the comics wasn't far  behind and in Avengers infinity war it's  revealed that the planet Zander which  housed the Nova Corps was destroyed by  Thanos a similar event happens in the  comic books  setting the lone surviving member of the  Nova Corps on a journey  to introduce one of the most powerful  Comics superheroes so why should Nova's  epic story be adapted for Disney Plus  simply puts guarding into the galaxy wet  bands appetites for more stories set in  the cosmic reaches of the Marvel  Universe some of the strangest and most  important comics take place on the  fringes of the Marvel galaxy and since  the third guardians film is set to bring  Peter Quill's story to an end we need  someone else out there exploring the  vast reaches of the cosmos so perhaps  it's time to open the space travel doors  in a way that's both accessible to the  audience and that expands the universe  even more this doesn't even run the risk  of brushing up against the main  storyline in the movie since it's a lot  easier to miss something g